IMPORT prelude

-- Foreign Recruiting Act 1875 (Singapore) -- what a "foreign State" is (s 2), the President's power to prohibit or permit one
-- person's recruiting by written order (s 3) and to prohibit or condition all recruiting by Gazette order (s 4), and the offence
-- of inducing recruits or aiding their engagement in violation of a prohibition or condition, with its penalty (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FRA1875.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". It carries no amendment
-- annotations; its Legislative History ends with the 2014 Revised Edition (operation 28 February 2014). The deposit's metadata calls
-- it the current version as at 1 October 2026. The Arrangement of Sections agrees with the body (ss 1 to 5).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0137 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act has five sections, so it is encoded whole except s 1 (short title).
--
-- Not encoded: the content of any order the President has made under s 3 or s 4 (none was looked for -- only whether one exists,
-- whom it binds and whether a condition was breached); what "service of any foreign State" covers beyond the principals listed
-- below (whether a foreign state-owned company or hospital counts is not decided by the text); whether s 5 reaches conduct outside
-- Singapore (the section does not say); any general law on fines or attempts that may supplement s 5; and any other Act (for
-- instance on terrorism or mercenaries) that may also catch the same conduct.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Foreign Recruiting Act 1875 -- recruiting`

§§ `2 -- foreign State`

-- s 2: "foreign State" "includes any person or persons exercising, or assuming to exercise, the powers of government in or over any
-- country, colony, province, or people beyond the limits of Singapore".
-- READING (an inference): "includes" extends the ordinary meaning of a foreign State (a foreign government) to de facto and
-- self-proclaimed authorities; it does not reach a private company or individual that claims no powers of government, nor the
-- Government of Singapore, which governs within, not beyond, the limits of Singapore.
DECLARE Principal IS ONE OF
    `a recognised foreign government`
    `persons exercising the powers of government over a foreign province`
    `an authority assuming to exercise the powers of government over a people abroad`
    `the Government of Singapore`
    `a private foreign company`
    `a foreign private individual`

GIVEN `the principal` IS A Principal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a foreign State` IF
    CONSIDER `the principal`
    WHEN `the Government of Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private foreign company` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a foreign private individual` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- order against or permission for one person`

-- s 3: "If any person is, within the limits of Singapore, obtaining, or attempting to obtain, recruits for the service of any foreign
-- State in any capacity, the President may by order in writing, signed by the Minister, either prohibit that person from so doing
-- or permit him to do so subject to any conditions which the President imposes."
DECLARE Recruitment HAS
    `recruiting for` IS A Principal
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the recruitment` IS A Recruitment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may make a section 3 order` IF
        `is a foreign State` (`the recruitment`'s `recruiting for`)
    AND `the recruitment`'s `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore`
    AND `the recruitment`'s `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits`

GIVEN `the order is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order is signed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 3 order is in proper form` IF
        `the order is in writing`
    AND `the order is signed by the Minister`

§§ `4 -- general order`

-- s 4: "The President may by general order notified in the Gazette either prohibit recruiting for the service of any foreign State,
-- or impose upon such recruiting any conditions which he thinks fit."
GIVEN `the order is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 4 general order is in proper form` IF
    `the order is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `5 -- the offence`

-- s 5: "Any person who in violation of the prohibition of the President, or of any condition subject to which permission to recruit
-- has been accorded -- (a) induces or attempts to induce any person to accept, agree to accept, or to proceed to any place with a
-- view of obtaining, any commission or employment in the service of any foreign State; or (b) knowingly aids in the engagement of
-- any person so induced by forwarding or conveying him, or by advancing money, or in any other way whatever, shall be guilty of an
-- offence".
-- READING (an inference): a s 3 order prohibits "that person" only, so it is treated as not putting anyone else in "violation of
-- the prohibition of the President". A s 4 general order binds everyone.
DECLARE OrderInForce IS ONE OF
    `no order`
    `a general prohibition notified in the Gazette under section 4`
    `a section 3 order prohibiting this person`
    `a section 3 order prohibiting another person only`
    `a permission or general conditions that this conduct breaches`
    `a permission or general conditions that this conduct complies with`

GIVEN `the order in force` IS A OrderInForce
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct violates a prohibition or condition` IF
    CONSIDER `the order in force`
    WHEN `a general prohibition notified in the Gazette under section 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a section 3 order prohibiting this person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a permission or general conditions that this conduct breaches` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `the order` IS A OrderInForce
    `the service is of` IS A Principal
    `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (a) is met` IF
        `is a foreign State` (`the conduct`'s `the service is of`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (b) is met` IF
        `is a foreign State` (`the conduct`'s `the service is of`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise`
    AND `the conduct`'s `acts knowingly`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits a section 5 offence` IF
        `the conduct violates a prohibition or condition` (`the conduct`'s `the order`)
    AND (    `limb (a) is met` `the conduct`
         OR  `limb (b) is met` `the conduct`)

§§ `5 -- penalty`

-- s 5: "shall be liable on conviction to a fine or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both."
-- The Act states no maximum fine.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS 7

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act states a maximum fine` MEANS FALSE

DECLARE Sentence IS ONE OF
    `a fine only`
    `imprisonment only`
    `a fine and imprisonment`

GIVEN `the sentence` IS A Sentence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a kind of sentence section 5 allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the sentence`
    WHEN `a fine only` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment only` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fine and imprisonment` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the imprisonment term is within section 5` IF
        `the term in years` > 0
    AND `the term in years` <= `the maximum imprisonment in years`
